License Notice
==============

ViruFunc Atlas v1.0 is staged for public release. Final code and data license
terms require project or institutional approval before publication.

Release decisions still to confirm:

- Code: an approved open-source license such as MIT, BSD-3-Clause, or
  Apache-2.0.
- Benchmark/resource data: an explicit data license such as CC-BY-4.0 or CC0,
  plus third-party source notices where required.
- Third-party resources: cite and follow the terms for NCBI/RefSeq/GenBank,
  UniProt, InterPro/Pfam/CDD, PHROG, Phold, Foldseek, PDB, ESM/ESMFold, and
  other external tools or databases used to rebuild optional artifacts.

No new sequence data were generated. The benchmark layer is derived from public
viral sequence records and includes frozen manifests, split definitions, label
rules, evaluator code, baseline/source tables, checksums, and reproducibility
metadata.
